  "qualification_limits": [
    "Timings observe the original viewport text followed by the next animation frame; they are a compositor proxy, not hardware display measurements. Clock uncertainty is included in conservative latency bounds.",
    "Healthy transport claims use one active answer and a controlled 100 ms producer on the local encrypted chain, 20 separate 600-character conversations. They are not WAN capacity or model inference benchmarks.",
    "The real work2-model run uses an isolated Linux Gateway to retain the production /dev/shm requirement, with the real macOS helper and original Electron renderer. Submit-to-first-visible includes model/workflow time.",
    "Long-text qualification uses 85 explicit harness scrolls to keep the answer tail visible. Automatic following, selection pause and focus require the desktop-experience branch and merged native validation.",
    "Recovery has one intentional hide during session replacement; the old preview is not displayed under a new session until its authority is verified. Healthy zero-blank requirements remain unchanged.",
    "Earlier same-conversation DOM-only samples do not establish viewport visibility and are superseded by the 20-sample viewport receipt.",
    "No independent send/receive/verification/paint per-layer timing breakdown was instrumented.",
    "Full Linux package testing preceded the last helper deadline sampling-order correction; focused helper race and vet checks cover that correction. Native fixtures were explicitly opted in and then committed separately."
